    "introduction": "Start at Highgate Underground’s Archway Road exit 3, on the public pavement clear of the exit. Press Start there: it plays the welcome immediately. This walk goes up to Highgate village, across the Heath, past 2 Willow Road and on to Keats House; the map continues to Hampstead Heath station. Allow about 85–100 minutes for 4.1 km, stories and looking. There are slopes, a short flight of steps, a narrow lane without continuous pavement, and shared paths. Public exteriors make the tour usable when the houses are closed. Keep the offline map handy at unnamed Heath forks. AI-assisted original writing and local AI narration by George; source notes and reconstruction bases are available in Read / directions.",
    "finishInstructions": "The final story is at Keats House. Tap End tour / stop location. For the mapped finish, continue along Keats Grove, right into South End Road, then follow the pavement and station signs to Hampstead Heath station (about 4 minutes). Hampstead Underground is the longer option: return along Keats Grove, left down Downshire Hill, then right along Rosslyn Hill/Hampstead High Street (about 14 minutes from Keats). Reviews and progress remain saved.",
